From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <plevickij57@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:30:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 71/71] pinctrl: qcom: ssbi-mpp: use the PM8901 register base

Unlike the other PM8xxx variants supported by this driver, PM8901 places
its MPP control registers at 0x27 rather than 0x50.  Using the common base
updates unrelated PMIC registers while the pinctrl cache misleadingly shows
the requested MPP state.

Select the PM8901 base when probing its compatible.  This lets MPP1 really
drive the external 5 V enable on Sony Hikari instead of leaving the hardware
at the bootloader-provided low state.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <plevickij57@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-ssbi-mpp.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-ssbi-mpp.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-ssbi-mpp.c
index 645a0f8fb..c51031358 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-ssbi-mpp.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-ssbi-mpp.c
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 
 /* MPP registers */
 #define SSBI_REG_ADDR_MPP_BASE		0x50
-#define SSBI_REG_ADDR_MPP(n)		(SSBI_REG_ADDR_MPP_BASE + n)
+#define SSBI_REG_ADDR_PM8901_MPP_BASE	0x27
 
 /* MPP Type: type */
 #define PM8XXX_MPP_TYPE_D_INPUT         0
@@ -839,6 +839,7 @@ static int pm8xxx_mpp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct pinctrl_pin_desc *pins;
 	struct gpio_irq_chip *girq;
 	struct pm8xxx_mpp *pctrl;
+	unsigned int reg_base = SSBI_REG_ADDR_MPP_BASE;
 	int ret;
 	int i;
 
@@ -849,6 +850,8 @@ static int pm8xxx_mpp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	pctrl->dev = &pdev->dev;
 	pctrl->npins = (uintptr_t) device_get_match_data(&pdev->dev);
 
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(pdev->dev.of_node, "qcom,pm8901-mpp"))
+		reg_base = SSBI_REG_ADDR_PM8901_MPP_BASE;
 	pctrl->regmap = dev_get_regmap(pdev->dev.parent, NULL);
 	if (!pctrl->regmap) {
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "parent regmap unavailable\n");
@@ -873,7 +876,7 @@ static int pm8xxx_mpp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < pctrl->desc.npins; i++) {
-		pin_data[i].reg = SSBI_REG_ADDR_MPP(i);
+		pin_data[i].reg = reg_base + i;
 
 		ret = pm8xxx_pin_populate(pctrl, &pin_data[i]);
 		if (ret)
-- 
